# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Never tracked. `.env.example` is the template that IS tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
*.pem
*.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Patient data and everything derived from it.
#
# `outputs/` is a scratch directory: the cohort CSV, every sub-CSV the data
# stage cuts from it, the matcher's column catalogue (all 1,394 names), and one
# folder per run. None of it belongs in a repository, and all of it is
# regenerable — see prep_hiv_dataset.py, make_sample_data.py, prep_nhanes.py and
# scripts/build_matcher_cache.py.
#
# The two entries below are the exceptions: the README explaining the folder,
# and the .gitkeep that keeps the empty folder present after a clone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
outputs/*
!outputs/.gitkeep
!outputs/README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `kg/`. Knowledge-graph dumps. AlzKB and AddictionKB are published elsewhere;
# these are 987MB of exports and their SQLite builds.
#
# Until 2026-09-23 this block ignored the payloads and kept the three scripts
# that produce and read them — build_sqlite.py twice and kg_to_okf.py. As of
# 2026-09-23, on explicit instruction, the whole folder is ignored and those
# three left the index. They are untouched on disk and still run here; a clone
# now has neither the payloads nor the code that builds them, so the path from
# a published graph to an OKF bundle is not reconstructable from a clone.
#
# The two payload patterns below are kept rather than folded into `kg/`. They
# are a separate decision — the payloads were never publishable, and if `kg/`
# is ever narrowed again they must not quietly come back with it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
kg/
kg/**/*.db
kg/**/*.cypherl

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reinstallable
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv
.venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

